id: pm-lint-sdk-settings-sections
title: Adopt SDK lint settings section reads
description: Replace private settings reopening and parsing with the public SDK section reader while retaining lint policy validation.
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-lint#66",sdk-adoption,settings
created_at: "2026-11-06T15:45:20.572Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-08T11:06:53.439Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Direct and registered command reads agree on policy; Malformed documents and sections produce typed SDK refusals; Absent policy, custom core schema and sibling sections remain compatible; Behavioral revert proofs and package gates pass"
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T15:45:26.020Z",codex-sol,"Scope: pm-lint only, companion pm-cli-website-m8dy (G4), audit pm-cli-website-7zcy. Replace the private readSettings plus raw-file parser with readSettingsSection and its validator callback. Keep lint rule vocabulary, numeric windows and CLI precedence because these are package policy. Test real non-git trackers and registered commands through createExtensionTestHarness; record behavioral revert proofs. SDK 2026.11.4 already exports the needed API; dependency pins stay unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T15:49:10.888Z",codex-sol,"Implementation: removed lintSettingsFromText and private readSettings/raw-file recovery. readSettingsSection validates stored lint policy with resolveConfig; repairs reuse readLintSettings while retaining raw bytes only for snapshot digest and schema fencing. SDK section APIs shipped in 2026.11.2, so peer/manifest minimums move there while the 2026.11.4 dev pin stays unchanged. Targeted build plus settings/repair tests passed 16/16. Revert proofs in a disposable package copy: reverting only readLintSettings makes the policy test fail with Missing expected rejection and malformed-document test fail on untyped SyntaxError (each 0/1); restoring that reader and reverting only repair policy parsing makes the policy test fail on untyped Expected a lint settings object (0/1). The fixed targeted suite is rerunning via linked pm tests."
  "2026-11-06T15:53:01.395Z",codex-sol,"Linked pm test rerun passed 16/16 after the disposable revert checks. npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run duplication (0 percent), and npm run docstring passed. Confirmed readSettingsSection in the public 2026.11.2 package declarations. Full npm gate is running, with Bun and isolated-HOME verification to follow serially. The PR will use branch lint-sdk-settings-sections; CI and bot review are required before orchestrator verification. No SDK gaps encountered. Item remains in_progress; releasing the implementation claim for handoff."
  "2026-11-06T15:54:27.857Z",codex-sol,"Local strict tracker health reports only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew:2026.11.4:2026.11.5:pm-github; history_drift, integrity, settings and storage checks pass. This is already tracked by pm-lint-managed-extension-health-skew, whose prior evidence distinguishes local managed-extension state from clean CI. No dependency bump or extension mutation is in scope; preserve the diagnostic and verify fresh CI."
  "2026-11-06T20:10:29.688Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR 66 after CodeRabbit review on f1b33bf. Both nitpicks are valid coverage additions: distinguish an absent settings document from an absent lint section, and assert typed malformed-document refusals through repair previews. No production behavior change is planned. Existing initial implementation, revert proofs and full npm/Bun/isolated-HOME gates remain complete; new checks and final-head CI will cover this review update."
  "2026-11-06T20:12:53.976Z",codex-sol,"PR 66 review round 1: addressed both CodeRabbit threads (4496601492 and 4496601505). Added a separate missing-document test: readLintSettings returns undefined, full lint and repair preview refuse, and neither recreates settings.json. Extended all five malformed-document cases to assert typed settings_section_document_malformed refusals through repair previews using a real SDK-created item. Settings tests passed 5/5; the linked build/settings/repair command passed 17/17 after restoration. Typecheck and lint passed. Disposable-copy revert proofs: the new missing-document test fails against the original reader with Tracker settings disappeared during lint read; reverting only repair policy parsing makes the expanded malformed-document test fail on untyped SyntaxError. Both mutants exited 1 with 0/1 passing. No production code changes. The previous npm/Bun/isolated-HOME full gates are complete; fresh exact-head CI will validate this test-only review update. Latest review body contained only these two inline findings, with no additional outside-diff findings."
  "2026-11-08T01:22:59.910Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched all three review threads and all comments; only PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc60vERC remains unresolved. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Verified missing settings reaches JSON.parse(null).schema and throws an untyped TypeError. Add an unsafe_repair refusal before parsing, preserve the settings_read boundary and schema fence, and require typed embedded and registered-command results plus zero source mutations on a real non-git tracker. Self-review the complete PR for similar nullable reads. Remote branch was current but two commits behind main; merge changes only conflict in generated CHANGELOG.md."
  "2026-11-08T01:24:20.689Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc60vERC: missing settings now refuses with RepairRefusal unsafe_repair and a restore-settings remedy before schema parsing; the settings_read boundary and present-document schema guard remain intact. Expanded the existing missing-document regression to assert the exact API refusal, boundary order, registered lint repair receipt (writes 0, exit_code 2), and identical complete source inventory on a real non-git tracker. Disposable-copy behavioral revert proof: removing only the new null guard makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"missing settings documents\" test/settings.test.ts fail 0/1 with TypeError reading schema from null, exit 1; restoring it passes 1/1, exit 0. The fixed settings suite passes 5/5; pm test --run --progress executes the linked build/settings/repairs command and passes 17/17. Whole-PR review checked SDK defaults, malformed-document and invalid-policy refusals, schema fencing and remaining nullable reads; no other instance introduced by this PR was found. Strict tracker health passes 9/10 checks and fails only the pre-existing managed pm-github SDK skew (2026.11.4 host versus 2026.11.7 managed extension), already tracked by pm-lint-managed-extension-health-skew; no history drift or pending merge receipts. Proceeding with serial full npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-08T01:34:10.328Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated-HOME npm run release:check passed: 192/192 tests, 11 suites, no failures/skips; 100/100/100/100 statements/branches/functions/lines across all 32 configured source files; packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1 passed. Identity 0 violations; typecheck and lint pass; duplication 0 percent (63 sources); docstrings 120/120 declarations; production audit 0 vulnerabilities; pack, changelog and publish-attestation checks pass. No timeouts or retries were needed for the gates. A disposable tracked-source snapshot with current tracker changes and isolated HOME passes pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers 10/10 checks with zero warnings; the normal profile retains only the separately tracked managed-extension skew. Full bun run release:check is now running serially. No pm CLI/SDK bug encountered; linked files already cover both changed files, and linked tests ran successfully without writing run artifacts to the source tracker."
  "2026-11-08T01:42:31.870Z",codex-agent,"Review round complete: PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc60vERC is valid and fixed with a typed unsafe_repair refusal before nullable settings parsing. Regression verifies API and registered-command receipts, boundary preservation and zero source changes. Behavioral guard-only revert fails 0/1 on the original TypeError; restored implementation passes 1/1, followed by the fixed linked suite at 17/17. Full npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass with isolated HOME and global Git configuration disabled: each has 192/192 measured tests and 1/1 packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance; each reports 100/100/100/100 coverage over 32 source files, zero identity violations, zero duplication and zero production vulnerabilities. Typecheck, lint, docstrings, build, packing, changelog and release-publish attestation all pass at unchanged thresholds. No gate timeout or retry occurred. Strict source-copy tracker health with isolated HOME passes 10/10 checks; ordinary profile health retains the known managed-extension SDK skew tracked separately. Main was merged in fe6f17a; no tracker history was rewritten. Whole-PR self-review found no further instance introduced by the change. Latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range findings. No SDK gap or new CLI defect encountered. Final code and tracker changes are ready for push and fresh CI; no review replies, thread resolutions, merge or release actions are part of this round. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; releasing only this agents claim."
  "2026-11-08T04:45:38.831Z",codex-agent,"Continuation for PR #66: remote head and package worktree match; origin/main is already included. One unresolved CodeRabbit finding PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc608suL is valid. General rule: every plan digest must bind the exact policy used to derive its questions, including asynchronous SDK read hooks. Auditing all digest/configuration consumers, SDK and command renderers, non-git trackers and packed Node/Bun paths; preserving prior fixes and append-only evidence."
  "2026-11-08T04:48:33.340Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc608suL: capture settings bytes, obtain SDK-validated policy, compare sections with order-independent deep equality, then derive questions and plan identity only on agreement. Hook-replaced malformed captured documents refuse as stale_revision; stable malformed documents retain typed SDK errors and missing documents retain unsafe_repair. Whole-package search found repair planning was the only separate raw-settings/policy digest; incremental checkpoints already hash the evaluated config and recheck it before publication, while ordinary lint and portable/witness paths do not certify separate raw policy bytes. Added a 34-policy adversarial matrix spanning every built-in rule, absent sections, failOn, enable/disable, severity, scope and parameters, across API and command handler; JSON/TOON refusal parity and zero source writes are asserted. Added equivalent-order/sibling compatibility and replaced-malformed-document cases plus packed Node/Bun hook regressions. Focused build/settings/repairs suite passed 19/19; typecheck, lint, duplication and docstrings passed. Disposable-copy revert proof: restoring only buildRepairPreview from the previous commit fails 0/1 with Missing expected rejection; removing only the deep-equality guard also fails 0/1; restored implementation passes 1/1 using node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"every repair policy\" test/repairs.test.ts. No production source was mutated for revert tests. Full npm/Bun gates follow serially at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-08T05:00:56.776Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME, disabled global/system Git configuration and credential-filtered child environment: 194/194 tests in 11 suites, 100/100/100/100 coverage across 32 configured source files, plus packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1 including shipped-code policy-hook regressions. Identity, typecheck, lint, duplication (zero), docstrings (120/120 declarations), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), build, pack, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. Linked pm test rerun passed 19/19 without recording run artifacts. Strict health on a disposable tracked-file copy passes 10/10 checks with one advisory telemetry queue notice; ordinary profile health retains only the known gate-failing managed pm-github SDK skew tracked separately. No new SDK gap or CLI defect found. Append-only history prefix against the previous branch head is preserved; this item does not yet exist on origin/main. Separate Bun release gate follows serially."
  "2026-11-08T05:19:30.744Z",codex-agent,"Final verification for PR #66 policy-binding review: both npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed serially with isolated HOME, global/system Git configuration disabled and at most two test workers. Each passed 194/194 tests in 11 suites with zero failures/skips and 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 32 configured source files, followed by packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1 including real policy-hook mutation cases. Identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, build, zero-vulnerability production audit, pack, changelog and publish-attestation gates all passed unchanged. No gate timeout or retry occurred; the existing model suite was slower on the Bun gate but completed. The focused linked command passed 19/19. Both disposable-copy revert proofs fail 0/1 and restore to 1/1. All rule-policy/digest paths were audited; the shared preview fix covers embedded API and command transports. Equivalent key ordering and sibling settings remain compatible; missing and malformed refusals remain intact. Fresh fetch confirms current main is included and the remote PR head is unchanged. No duplicate item or PR, no rewritten history, no review replies/resolutions, no merge/release, and no new CLI/SDK gap. Remaining handoff gates are fresh pushed-head CI and orchestrator re-review; the known ordinary-profile managed-extension skew remains tracked separately. Releasing only this implementation claim while retaining in_progress status for verification."
  "2026-11-08T10:39:19.119Z",codex-agent,"Continuation: remote head 0bfb76a matches the clean package worktree and contains current main. Only unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc60-KzO remains; latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Valid defect class: every configuration input consumed by a certified repair must match the captured settings, and later SDK hooks must not replace already-fenced schema. Preserve prior fixes, sibling-setting compatibility and append-only tracker evidence. Audit all SDK, CLI, JSON/TOON and packed Node/Bun consumers; add hook-interleaving regressions on non-git trackers and behavioral revert proof."
  "2026-11-08T10:42:37.457Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc60-KzO. General rule: captured configuration must cover every core input used by fenced schema reads and repair certification. Compare schema before loading references, compare all SDK-recognized core keys without duplicating a key registry, and run subsequent reads/planning/validation in an isolated extension scope to prevent late hook edits including ABA. Unrelated sibling sections and equivalent key ordering remain compatible. Whole-package audit found this separate raw-settings/schema fence only in repairs; ordinary lint has no separate raw digest, incremental checkpoints hash and recheck the evaluated config/status registry, and other digest paths hash their actual input. Shared preview covers SDK, command and JSON/TOON receipts; new packed Node/Bun regressions exercise schema-only and delayed hooks. Existing tests retained; common receipt assertions were extracted to satisfy unchanged zero duplication. Focused settings/repairs pass 22/22. Disposable-copy behavioral revert: previous builder fails all 3 new tests (0/3); removing only isolation fails 2/3; restored builder passes 3/3. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"every core setting|repair schema remains isolated|repair settings recheck\" test/repairs.test.ts. No source checkout was mutated for revert checks. Full serial npm/Bun gates follow."
  "2026-11-08T10:55:53.448Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME, disabled global/system Git configuration, credential-filtered children and at most two test workers: 197/197 tests across 11 suites; 100/100/100/100 coverage over all 32 configured source files; packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1 including schema-only and delayed-hook regressions. Identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings (120/120), production audit (zero vulnerabilities), build, package contents, changelog and release-publish attestation all passed unchanged. The full gate completed in 660 seconds without timeout/retry. Linked pm test --run --progress passed 22/22 with evidence recording explicitly disabled. CI-equivalent tracked-file snapshot health passed 10/10 checks with strict exit, required merge drivers and zero warnings. Separate Bun release gate follows serially."
  "2026-11-08T11:06:52.394Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 verification for PR #66: thread PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc60-KzO is valid and fixed across the shared repair builder. Schema changes refuse before reference loading; all SDK-recognized core inputs are bound to captured settings; subsequent SDK reads, planning and validation are isolated from late hooks. Equivalent ordering and unrelated sibling settings remain compatible. Package-wide class audit covers SDK/CLI, JSON/TOON, non-git trackers and packed consumers; no other separate captured-settings/schema-fence path exists. Revert proof: previous builder fails 3/3 new regressions, removing isolation fails 2/3, restored builder passes 3/3. Focused and linked tests pass 22/22. Serial npm run release:check (660 seconds) and bun run release:check (633 seconds) each pass 197/197 tests in 11 suites, 100/100/100/100 coverage on all 32 configured sources, and packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance 1/1. Identity, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 120/120 docstrings, build, zero-vulnerability production audit, packing, changelog and release attestation pass unchanged. No full-gate timeout or retry. Strict tracked-file snapshot health passes 10/10 checks with required merge drivers and zero warnings. The declared 2026.11.2 minimum SDK exports the isolation API; dependency pins stay unchanged. Fresh fetch confirms main is included and the remote branch is unchanged; all PR commit emails match the required bot identity. No new CLI/SDK defect, duplicate item/PR, history rewrite, review reply/resolution, merge or release. Releasing only this implementation claim and retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification. Fresh pushed-head CI and re-review remain required: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/66/checks."
